section.p:
        To use the SList: 

        In the Model, set up getter methods for the ArrayList and the selected member object: 

private ArrayList customers = new ArrayList(); 
private Customer selectedCustomer; 

public ArrayList getCustomers() { 
    return customers; 
} 

public Customer getSelectedCustomer() { 
    return selectedCustomer; 
} 

public void setSelectedCustomer(Customer inCustomer) { 
    selectedCustomer = inCustomer; 
} 


        In the view, create the SList and map it to the model getData methods: 

SList l = new SList(); 
l.setSelector("customers"); 
l.setRendererSelector("name");//within the Customer object, there is a public String getName() method to which we are mapping. 
l.setSelectionSelector("selectedCustomer"); 
l.setChangeSelectionControlID(ListController.SELECTED); 
JScrollPane left = new JScrollPane(l); 


         In the controller, if you wish to handle the ChangeSelection event on the SList, you must catch the SELECTED control in the doHandle method. 

protected void doHandleControl(Control inControl) throws ControlException { 
  if (inControl.matchesID(SELECTED)) { 
    doSelected(); 
  } 
}
